From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: llama: split decode for batches with supplied embedding rows

llama_decode_prepare also accepts batches of tokens and supplied embedding
rows (llama_batch.embd_input), whose outputs only need to be in batch order
(rows without one may sit between them), so a batching server can build its
next prefill pass while the previous one runs. llama_decode_launch now
extracts the NextN rows (host or device) like llama_decode, through one shared
helper, so a prepared pass feeds the MTP drafter, and the sampling transaction
begins in llama_decode_prepare, before the inputs are set, so samplers with
several outputs per sequence draw from the same generator state as in
llama_decode.

Upstream: not planned (batched serving path).

